{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And I have given you.</b> And I — behold, I truly did not transfer any inheritance at all when I gave you <b>one portion beyond your brothers</b> in the land, even though it is the land of your fathers, except that I gave you what <b>I took from the hand</b> of him who is <b>an Amorite</b> in his evil deeds, and a man of mere talk who says much yet does not even do a little to do good — and this is Esau, from whom I acquired the birthright. For were it not for this, your brothers would not have had so great a share in the inheritance of the fathers in the land." "<b>With my sword and with my bow.</b> With my wisdom and understanding, which are the sword and bow of the righteous, as it says: חֲגוֹר חַרְבְּךָ עַל יָרֵךְ גִּבּוֹר (Psalms 45:4). Our Rabbis of blessed memory have already explained (Shabbat 63a) that this is written concerning words of Torah. And conversely in the same sense: שִׁנֵּיהֶם חֲנִית וְחִצִּים וּלְשׁוֹנָם חֶרֶב חַדָּה (Psalms 57:5), and likewise: וַיִּדְרְכוּ אֶת לְשׁוֹנָם קַשְׁתָּם שֶׁקֶר (Jeremiah 9:2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:14.926384424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}